WEBVTT

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.250
In June 2026, China did something small

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:05.400
that changed a very big market.

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:07.390
It added two American companies to its

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:10.640
export control list, MP Materials and USA

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:12.040
Rare Earth.

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:14.030
Those two names matter because they are

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:15.870
the center of America's plan to build a

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.850
Rare Earth supply chain outside China.

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:21.300
By naming them, Beijing was not banning

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:22.720
anything outright.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:24.360
It was showing exactly where the leverage

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:25.020
sits.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:26.920
This is the question we are going to

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:27.400
unpack.

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:29.050
Why can a small set of choke points affect

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.610
cars, chips, and even defense?

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:33.510
The short answer is that the world's Rare

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:36.280
Earth supply runs through a gate, and one

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:37.640
country holds the keys.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.900
Start with the materials themselves.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:42.440
Rare Earths are a family of 17 elements

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:44.690
you have probably never heard of, but they

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:47.150
are inside almost everything electric.

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:49.440
The magnets in electric vehicle motors,

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:51.840
the turbines in wind farms, the guidance

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.240
systems in defense hardware, the vibration

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:56.600
motor in your phone, they are called rare,

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:58.740
but they are not actually scarce in the

00:00:58.740 --> 00:00:59.380
ground.

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:01.400
The leverage is not in the mining.

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:02.830
It is in the processing.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:04.960
Here is the number that matters.

00:01:04.990 --> 00:01:07.160
China mines a large share of the world's

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:10.480
Rare Earths around 70%, but it processes

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:13.230
an even bigger share, roughly 90% of

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:15.710
global separation capacity, and close to

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:18.100
99% of the heavy Rare Earths used in the

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:19.760
most demanding magnets.

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:21.760
So when a country exports raw ore and

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:23.890
imports refined magnets, it has already

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:25.360
passed through one gate.

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:28.160
That gate is Chinese separation capacity.

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:29.810
This is the definition we need.

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:31.570
A choke point is not the mine.

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:33.560
It is the gate after the mine, the

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:36.100
refinery, the separator, the magnet maker,

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:38.270
where a handful of facilities concentrate

00:01:38.270 --> 00:01:39.320
world supply.

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:41.480
Think of the chain as four steps.

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:43.570
First, the mine, ore comes out of the

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:46.100
ground in California, Australia, Myanmar,

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:47.090
and elsewhere.

00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:49.560
Second, the refinery, that ore is crushed,

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:51.720
separated, and turned into individual

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:52.360
oxides.

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:54.800
This is the hard, dirty, capital-intensive

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.760
step, and it is where China holds its

00:01:57.110 --> 00:01:57.550
position.

00:01:57.590 --> 00:01:59.950
Third, the magnet, the oxides become the

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:01.960
permanent magnets inside motors and

00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:03.000
generators.

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:05.620
Fourth, the factory, those magnets go into

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:08.560
cars, wind turbines, robots, and weapons.

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:11.170
Each step passes value to the next, and at

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:13.170
step two, most of the world's ore stops

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:14.400
for processing.

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:16.650
Here is what that concentration looks like

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:17.400
in prices.

00:02:17.430 --> 00:02:19.920
Neodymium praseodymium oxide, the key

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:22.440
feedstock for permanent magnets, opened

00:02:22.510 --> 00:02:25.880
2026 near $53 a kilogram.

00:02:25.910 --> 00:02:29.900
By July, spot quotes were above $110.

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:32.320
China's Rare Earth price index reached

00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:33.240
270.

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:38.050
Five on 24 July, 2026, about 170% above

00:02:38.390 --> 00:02:40.620
its 2010 baseline.

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:42.890
Prices stopped being a market story and

00:02:42.890 --> 00:02:44.640
became a policy story.

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:46.290
That is why markets care.

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:48.780
The sectors that depend on these magnets

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:49.740
are enormous.

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:51.800
The International Energy Agency has

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:54.410
pointed to the huge value of output that

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:57.110
is directly exposed to magnet supply on

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:59.310
the order of $6.5 trillion.

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:01.250
A shock at the choke point does not stay

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:02.720
in the mining sector.

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:05.050
It ripples into electric vehicles, into

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:07.320
wind energy, into the cost of the energy

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.650
transition, and into defense procurement.

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:11.860
So what is the West doing about it?

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:15.060
In February, 2026, the United States

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:17.760
launched FORGE, a 54-nation alliance

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:21.030
backed by Project Vault, a $12 billion

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:23.130
fund, to rebuild critical minerals supply

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:24.710
chains outside China.

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:26.810
MP Materials has a partnership with the

00:03:26.810 --> 00:03:28.780
Department of Defense to build domestic

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:30.200
magnet production.

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:31.450
That is the plan.

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:33.520
Here is the honest uncertainty.

00:03:33.550 --> 00:03:35.840
Rebuilding separation capacity is not like

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:37.280
reopening a mine.

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:38.480
It takes years.

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:40.610
Analysts say a realistic timeline for

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:42.880
meaningful Western separation runs to the

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:45.120
end of the decade, and full independence

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:47.250
could take 20 to 30 years.

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:49.680
The infrastructure, the chemistry, and the

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:51.670
skilled labor all have to be built from a

00:03:51.670 --> 00:03:52.350
small base.

00:03:52.390 --> 00:03:54.600
So the race is not against a deadline.

00:03:54.630 --> 00:03:57.220
It is against a gate that already exists.

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:59.510
The signal to watch is not the headline

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:00.140
price.

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:02.240
It is the behavior underneath it.

00:04:02.270 --> 00:04:03.880
Watch whether new separation plants

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:06.870
outside China actually come online.

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:08.950
Watch whether Western automakers and

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:11.260
defense buyers sign long-term magnet

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:14.000
contracts at higher prices or keep buying

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:14.520
spot.

00:04:14.550 --> 00:04:16.410
Watch whether the entity list grows from

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:19.490
10 American firms in June to 14 European

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:21.460
firms in July, because that tells you the

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:23.980
choke point is being used deliberately.

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:26.100
The mine was never the story.

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:28.160
The gate was always the story.

00:04:28.190 --> 00:04:30.600
One country, a small set of facilities,

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:33.250
and a 17-element family of metals that the

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:35.630
modern economy cannot build without.

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:37.240
That is the leverage.

00:04:37.270 --> 00:04:40.200
And in 2026, it has a price tag.

00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:41.850
The question for the next phase of the

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:44.920
global economy is not whether rare earths

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:45.600
matter.

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:47.790
It is whether the world can build a second

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:49.780
gate before the first one closes.
